art failure characterized by dyssynchrony: a pre-defined analysis from the CARE-HF trial</article-title><source>Eur Heart J</source><year>2007</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>1827</fpage><lpage>34</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17540848</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/eurheartj/ehm192</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bleeker</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaandorp</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lamb</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Boersma</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Steendijk</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>de Roos</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Wall</surname><given-names>EE van der</given-names></name><name><surname>Schalij</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bax</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of posterolateral scar tissue on clinical and echocardiographic improvement after cardiac resynchronization therapy</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>2006</year><volume>113</volume><fpage>969</fpage><lpage>976</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16476852</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.105.543678</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lim</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Bars</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitchell-Heggs</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Roiron</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Elbaz</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamdaoui</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Lellouche</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Dubois